  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the man as the embodiment of the stereotypes",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the man (person with surprised expression) because the meme uses him as a visual stand-in for 'white people' as defined by the surrounding text. The spatial arrangement and the top text 'things white people do' create a direct mapping where the viewer is invited to see the man as the subject of the derogatory claims, thus projecting the user's identity onto him as the target of the stereotypes.",
